# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 gen.cc pow, "extract integral powers in a product exponent". b^(n*s/d), with n an integer and d an integer denominator in a product exponent, is rewritten as ((b^s)^(1/d))^r*(b^s)^q (n = q*d+r), which is b^(n*s/d) only when im(s*ln(b)) lies in (-pi,pi] (for a negative b in complex mode Giac takes (-b)^s and exp(i*pi*s/d), so im(s*ln(-b))): 2^sqrt(-1-10^-3), Giac's 2^(10*i*sqrt(10010)/1000), became (2^(10*i*sqrt(10010)))^(1/1000), the principal root of 2^(1000.5*i), about 0.999997254512+0.00234328161588*i (right 0.769017463424+0.639227769225*i); also 2^sqrt(-2-10^-3), 3^sqrt(-1-10^-9). Takes the rule only where it holds: s = 1 always keeps it, whatever b is (arg b lies in (-pi,pi], and an integer power of the principal root is the principal power: (-pi)^(3/2) = sqrt(-pi)*(-pi), sqrt(acosh(-1/2)^2), (-1-i/10^20)^(1/2) and the root in asinh(-10^300) keep sqrt as before); otherwise it is decided on the doubles of b and s with a margin at the cut (as patch 0018), except for a negative real b with a real s (the CAS view, complex mode off), where im(s*ln(b)) = s*pi and the rule holds for -1 < s < 1, realness by Giac's is_real where the doubles are near the axis (acosh(-2) = ln(-sqrt(3)-2) as before); elsewhere the power stays as typed and its evalf is the principal value. b or s with no numeric value or a non-finite double part (asinh(-10^1250)), and every rule with r = 0 (an integer power), keep today's form (2^(i/1000) = (2^i)^(1/1000), 2^(sqrt(2)/7) = (2^sqrt(2))^(1/7)).
